### I CANNOT SOLVE THIS

This is Erdős Problem 779 — the Deaconescu conjecture — which is explicitly marked `category research open` in the problem statement. It is an unsolved research-level conjecture in number theory. The statement asserts that for every $n \geq 1$, with $P = \prod_{i=0}^{n} p_i$ (the primorial of the first $n+1$ primes), there exists a prime $p$ with $p_n < p < P$ such that $P + p$ is also prime.

No proof is known. The problem text itself only references known partial computational results (verified for $n \leq 1000$) and a secondary conjecture $p \leq n^{O(1)}$; none of this constitutes a leaked solution. I cannot prove an open conjecture.
